  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Mississippi received $72.2M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The state logged 3,406 awards with an average award size of $21.2K. Obligations fell 98.9% year over year. Fiscal-year totals prior to FY2027 show larger activity: FY22 recorded $5.2B, FY23 recorded $8.8B, FY24 recorded $6.4B, FY25 recorded $8.2B, and FY26 recorded $6.4B. The Department of Veterans Affairs led buying in FY2027 to date with $46.8M in obligations, followed by the Department of Homeland Security with $6.4M and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration with $6M. Contractors receiving the largest obligations in FY2027 to date include SPATIAL FRONT INC with $6.5M, COLUMBUS MARBLE WORKS, INC. with $5.4M, and PARAMOUNT CONSTRUCTION GROUP, LLC with $4.9M. Cut Stone and Stone Product Manufacturing is the top industry by obligations with $8.9M, followed by All Other Outpatient Care Centers with $7.9M and Computer Systems Design Services with $6.7M.",
